## script that wrote this log
    #!/usr/bin/env bash
    # Milestone 3 part 6 P2 run.log (specs/0028-images-and-comments-second-
    # half.md, "P2: the anchors and the removal" and "Harness runs",
    # `--anchor-sample`, `--remove-image-sample` and the run log's own check,
    # anchor and removeimage bullets; planning rulings during P2, 1 to 3):
    #   1. the release binaries built at the phase commit on both targets and
    #      hashed;
    #   2. before the run, the survey of the corpus (imgsurvey.py, expat without
    #      namespace processing for W and its drawing part, ids and counts only,
    #      the corpus directory its parameter): per workbook W's images by the
    #      read's rules and of each anchor kind, its drawing's root children,
    #      the media entries, W's drawing, an empty drawing, W's and the
    #      drawing's rels parts, the media entries the removal of the first
    #      image drops by the spec's count rule, and the calculation chain; the
    #      corpus's drawing parts and the largest drawing's anchor count
    #      (decision 8); its forms checked; its counts later checked against
    #      every tool line;
    #   3. the corpus's workbooks holding xl/calcChain.xml counted (specs/0025
    #      P3 verification ruling 4), and TMPDIR for the corpus runs made on the
    #      disk under <work>, its device and the corpus directory's printed and
    #      compared;
    #   4. the corpus runs with --tool-arg --anchor-sample and --tool-arg
    #      --remove-image-sample on both targets, each recorded as
    #      m3p6-p2-<sample>-<utc-date>-<shortsha>.md and .txt, the record
    #      checked against its run directory table by table; every row ok;
    #   5. the run log's own comparison (imgcmp.py, python3, zipfile, byte spans
    #      and ElementTree, printed below) over every output of both labels of
    #      both samples: for the anchor sample M2 part 4d P3's image checks
    #      carried for two anchors and the spec's anchor checks (the twoCellAnchor
    #      with editAs oneCell, the absoluteAnchor with pos 914400 by 914400 and
    #      ext 38100 by 38100, the kept children byte-identical); for the
    #      removal the spec's removeimage checks (the drawing's root children
